KG42.register("rules-c3e5398b61a0a4f11ed1180e",{"id":"18-dlmp_analysis::v141-c-R001","paper":"18-dlmp_analysis","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R001","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local market clearing","process_stage":"clearing","market_meaning":"DSOs perform local market clearing in the low-voltage grid. Scope: Low-voltage local markets in the common TSO-DSO approach described in the paper. Condition: Given the TLMP of the corresponding transmission buses. Low-voltage clearing must allow reserves to be delivered by distributed resources while respecting distribution line and voltage limits. Scope: The low-voltage markets proposed by Caramanis et al., clearing real power, reactive power and reserves.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function clearing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["clearing.local","coordination.local_operator"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R001-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"clearing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Low-voltage local markets in the common TSO-DSO approach described in the paper. | The low-voltage markets proposed by Caramanis et al., clearing real power, reactive power and reserves.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E003"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"DSOs perform local market clearing in the low-voltage grid. Scope: Low-voltage local markets in the common TSO-DSO approach described in the paper. Condition: Given the TLMP of the corresponding transmission buses.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Low-voltage clearing must allow reserves to be delivered by distributed resources while respecting distribution line and voltage limits. Scope: The low-voltage markets proposed by Caramanis et al., clearing real power, reactive power and reserves.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E002","location":{"location_id":"src-b1966ef5f7-p01-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. Introduction","anchor_text":"aspect of electricity market design. The relevance of dis- tributed resources is expected to increas","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Caramanis et al. [4] propose (i) a transmission system market that trades real power and reserves, and (ii) low-voltage markets that clear real power, reactive power and reserves, such that the reserves can be delivered by distributed resources while respecting distribution line limits and voltage limits."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E003","location":{"location_id":"src-b1966ef5f7-p01-c2r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. Introduction","anchor_text":"ure p , p , he such that the reserves can be delivered by distributed resources uf- while respecting","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A related question is how distribution locational marginal prices should be computed. In this respect, the common approach adopted in [4], [7], and [11]–[14] is the following: (i) locational marginal prices of high-voltage buses (TLMPs) are determined by clearing transmission markets, and (ii) DSOs clear local markets in the low-voltage grid in order to determine distribution locational marginal prices (DLMPs) for real power at the level of individual distribution nodes, given the TLMP of the corresponding transmission buses."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"This procedural rule's evidence describes an institutional clearing step and a cited proposal; it introduces no decision variable within the scope of the frozen nodes clearing.local and coordination.local_operator. Symbols such as p_i, q_i, f_i, l_i and v_i are defined only in the separate OPF formulation of mechanism v141-a-M03 and are not imported here.","empty_theta_reason":"The evidence for this rule does not define any parameter with a symbol, value or unit. TLMP is mentioned only as an externally given conditioning price, and DLMPs are outcomes of clearing; no numeric coefficients, capacities, limits or constants are specified in this rule's scope."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E003","quote":"DSOs clear local markets in the low-voltage grid in order to determine distribution locational marginal prices (DLMPs) for real power at the level of individual distribution nodes, given the TLMP of the corresponding transmission buses."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E002","quote":"low-voltage markets that clear real power, reactive power and reserves, such that the reserves can be delivered by distributed resources while respecting distribution line limits and voltage limits."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"2ab939de36e0e49e53ca39b7156278d2c825a6a235ff05555932bcda4839e924","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule is a procedural description of local market clearing in the introduction. Its exact evidence states which markets DSOs clear, which products a cited low-voltage market proposal clears, and that reserves must be deliverable while respecting distribution line and voltage limits. The evidence for this rule contains no equation, objective function, constraint algebra, variable definition, parameter value, unit, or explicit optimization formulation bound to clearing.local or coordination.local_operator. The paper's formal OPF and DLMP equations belong to mechanism v141-a-M03 and its separate rules, so they cannot be imported into this rule. B evidence remains unreviewed; this formalization does not assert verified source correctness.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","clearing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R001-E001"],"rationale":"Constraint C001 states that DSOs perform local market clearing in the low-voltage grid. In the frozen graph this is represented by the edge from coordination.local_operator to clearing.local, with evidence v141-b-g01-E003 stating that DSOs clear local markets given the TLMP of the corresponding transmission buses."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-C002","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Constraint C002 concerns the product and feasibility scope of low-voltage clearing: clearing real power, reactive power and reserves such that reserves can be delivered while respecting distribution line and voltage limits. It binds to the clearing.local node. The frozen rule graph has no separate edge for this product-scope statement, so no edge is asserted."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
